#10;VARIANT:&#10;NM_001267550.2:c.61328A&gt;G&#10;INHERITANCE:&#10;Autosomal dominant" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="true" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[0,571][64,2590]" drawing-order="0" hint="" /><node index="1" text="" resource-id="" class="android.view.View" package="com.szalongevity.sza_mobile" content-desc="MONITOR CLOSELY&#10;Aneurysm-osteoarthritis syndrome&#10;GENE:&#10;SMAD3&#10;VARIANT:&#10;NM_005902.4:c.533-13_533-10del&#10;INHERITANCE:&#10;Autosomal dominant" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="true" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[64,571][1216,2590]" drawing-order="0" hint=""><node index="0" text="" resource-id="" class="android.widget.ScrollView" package="com.szalongevity.sza_mobile" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="true" focused="false" scrollable="true" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[77,1283][1203,2564]" drawing-order="0" hint=""><node index="0" text="" resource-id="" class="android.view.View" package="com.szalongevity.sza_mobile" content-desc="Managing Aneurysm-osteoarthritis syndrome requires a holistic lifestyle approach for effective prevention and symptom management. A crucial aspect of managing this condition involves regular medical check-ups and monitoring to detect any changes or complications early. Exercise and physical activity should be tailored to the individual's abilities and limitations, with guidance from healthcare professionals to avoid injury. Maintaining a healthy diet, rich in nutrients and low in inflammatory foods, can help alleviate symptoms and improve overall health. Additionally, avoiding smoking and limiting alcohol consumption are essential lifestyle modifications that can significantly reduce the risk of complications. Furthermore, stress management techniques, such as meditation, yoga, and mindfulness, can help improve symptoms and enhance quality of life. Genetic counseling may also be beneficial in understanding the risk of passing on the condition to family members and developing personalized prevention strategies. Overall, a comprehensive lifestyle approach, in collaboration with healthcare professionals, is crucial for effective management and prevention of Aneurysm-osteoarthritis syndrome." checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="true" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[142,1283][1138,1712]" drawing-order="0" hint="" /><node index="1" text="" resource-id="" class="android.view.View" package="com.szalongevity.sza_mobile" content-desc="Epidemiology" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="true" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[142,1803][446,1868]" drawing-order="0" hint="" /><node index="2" text="" resource-id="" class="android.view.View" package="com.szalongevity.sza_mobile" content-desc="Aneurysm-osteoarthritis syndrome (AOS) is a rare genetic disorder characterized by the development of aneurysms in various parts of the body, particularly in the aorta and cerebral arteries, as well as osteoarthritis. With an estimated prevalence of around 1-3 in a million individuals worldwide, AOS exhibits autosomal dominant inheritance, although sporadic cases have also been reported. The age of onset and severity of symptoms can vary widely, even among family members with the same genetic mutation. Both men and women can be affected, and the disorder has been reported in individuals of diverse ethnic backgrounds. The combination of aneurysms and osteoarthritis in AOS can lead to a range of clinical manifestations, including pain, mobility limitations, and potential life-threatening complications such as rupture of aneurysms or dissection. As a result, early and accurate diagnosis and ongoing management are crucial for individuals with AOS." checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="true" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[142,1953][1138,2564]" drawing-order="0" hint="" /></node></node><node index="2" text="" resource-id="" class="android.view.View" package="com.szalongevity.sza_mobile" content-desc="MONITOR CLOSELY&#10;Dilated cardiomyopathy 1G&#10;GENE:&#10;TTN&#10;VARIANT:&#10;NM_001267550.2:c.61328A&gt;G&#10;INHERITANCE:&#10;Autosomal dominant" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="true" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[1216,571][1280,2590]" drawing-order="0" hint="" /></node></node><node NAF="true" index="4" text="" resource-id="" class="android.view.View" package="com.szalongevity.sza_mobile" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="true" enabled="true" focusable="true" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[575,2668][705,2694]" drawing-order="0" hint="" /></node></node></node></node></node></node></node></node></node></hierarchy>